    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "1.2 Notations Description"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000030",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0007-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0007-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0006",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0007-l0000",
      "p0002-n0007-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "Total time cost: The average time interval for a vehicle from the beginning point of the detection area to the ending point of the detection area is the total time cost."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000031",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0008-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0008-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0008-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0008-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0006",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0008-l0000",
      "p0002-n0008-l0001",
      "p0002-n0008-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "Theoretical time cost:  If there is only one vehicle in the system and that vehicle is not limited by the control signal, the time interval for that vehicle from the beginning point of the detection area to the ending point of the detection area is the theoretical time cost."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000032",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0009-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0009-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0006",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0009-l0000",
      "p0002-n0009-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "Time delayed: The difference between the total time cost and the theoretical time cost is the Time delayed."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000033",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0006",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0010-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "L: the number of lanes in each direction of the highway."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000034",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0006",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0010-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "B: the total number of tollbooths in each direction."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000035",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0007",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "1.3 Our Work"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000036",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0012-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0007",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0012-l0000",
      "p0002-n0012-l0001",
      "p0002-n0012-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "With the popularization of ETC equipment and autonomous vehicles, the MTC lanes will be totally replaced by the ETC lanes in the next 20 years, which will increase the road capacity and decrease the time cost by each car passing through the toll station."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000037",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0002-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0002-n0013-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0007",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0013-l0000",
      "p0002-n0013-l0001",
      "p0002-n0013-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "At present the traditional design of toll stations covers a large area, and the cost of construction is high. With the raise of the vehicles' speed, there will be congestions at the merging point, which may increase the possibility of accident."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000038",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "merged_block_id": "b000040",
        "operation": "cross_page_join_candidate"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0001-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0001-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0003-n0001-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0003-n0001-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0007",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0014-l0000",
      "p0003-n0001-l0000",
      "p0003-n0001-l0001",
      "p0003-n0001-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2,
      3
    ],
    "text": "\u2460 We designed a cellular toll booth model, designed its shape, size and merge. In order to make the cellular toll booth more adaptable to practical application, we escalated from the aspects of the area, the throughput, the accident prevention, the hybrid lane and the only ETC lane, self-driving vehicle and so on."
  }
]
